  "query_preview": "../Saturday through Tuesday/...\nLong range forecast remains on track; Sunday remains a favorable \nday, with lighter winds and perhaps seeing a bit of low angle sun \naction. Will have to monitor fog potential over Sunday, stay \ntuned. Outflow winds build Sunday night. Primary forecast \nchallenge Wednesday night is diagnosing a shortwave trough moving \nthrough the gulf Saturday, shearing apart as it hits the coast \nbringing in some precipitation. As of Wednesday night, our \nforecast for Saturday shows no snow accumulation for communities \nalong the Icy Strait Corridor with the snow level likely near \n1000ft to 2000ft (for Icy Strait to Taku). For Haines and Skagway \nprimary impact will be on upper elevation passes, with the \nlimiting factor for Haines the southwesterly flow coming across \nthe Chilkat Range. For White Pass will have to watch how far north\nhigher moisture can sneak in. Current forecast has an inch or two\nheading up the hill near the pass Friday into Saturday. Current \nguidance has higher moisture in the central Panhandle, if this can\nsneak north a bit it would bring a few more inches of snow. Stay \ntuned.",
